% The main proof for two disjoint edges (pattern.lad) into the path 0-1-2-3
% (target.lad), written by hand for phase 2 of dev_docs/decomposition-counting.md:
% from the solver's encoding (input.opb), whose preserved set is the x variables, to
% the translator's counting formula for statement (output.opb), whose preserved set is
% its own y variables. Check with
%   veripb --force-checked-deletion input.opb main.pbp output.opb
% which should say "s VERIFIED OUTPUT EQUIENUMERABLE". The gate ids are the node ids
% in statement, so this proof only fits that statement.
